{
  "id": "question-words-a1",
  "level": "a1",
  "area": "Every day",
  "title": "Question words: What, Where, When, Who, How",
  "tagline": "The small words that start every question — ask about anything, anyone, anywhere.",
  "cefr": "A1",
  "exam": [
    "Speaking Part 1 — questions about you and your life",
    "Writing Part 6 — a short email"
  ],
  "why": "In Speaking Part 1 the examiner asks you six or seven questions — <i>Where do you live? What's your favourite sport?</i> — and every one starts with a question word. The same little words help you write emails and understand notices. Learn these eight words and you can ask about anything.",
  "hook": {
    "text": "Sofia is doing a school project on a video call. \"<b>Where</b> do you live, Liam? <b>What's</b> your favourite food? <b>How old</b> is your sister?\" Liam laughs. \"One question at a time, Sofia!\"",
    "ask": "Can you find three different question words in the story? What is each one asking about — a place, a thing or an age?"
  },
